<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abellinum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abellinum was an ancient town of the Hirpini in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, at modern Atripalda, next to Avellino, which takes its name from it. It became a Roman colony, and its remains include walls, houses and an early Christian cemetery. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its people moved to the hill where Avellino now stands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abellinum.jpg" alt="Abellinum" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Costangelopacilio · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campanile_del_Duomo_e_Torre_dell%27Orologio_al_tramonto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
